[#AF87FF]claim-marker[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Durable held-claim artifact marker' section: record a held claim in a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dedicated `bead_claim.json` artifact file, write and clear it from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runner, and make the shutdown release funnel read it instead of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]depending only on runner process memory.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bidirectional claim reconciler[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]chop-acquire[dim] · [dim][/dim]after claim-recovery, claim-marker[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Bidirectional claim reconciler' section: give the bead_claim_checks [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chop an acquire pass that claims beads for live unpromoted unmarked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents, keeping the zero-candidate tick free of bead-store reads and the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]release pass's ordering invariant intact.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end verification and guidance[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify-and-document[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chop-acquire[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'End-to-end verification and guidance' section: add the integration test[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that reproduces the original failure, add the inverse doctor advisory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for unclaimed live pre-launch agents, and document that claims are [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]acquired best-effort and reconciled.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-94","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-94.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-f27b7f5f1dad01847dd184afd16d5fe2","started_at":"2026-07-25T11:37:51.037300+00:00","state":"completed"}],"schema_version":2,"s